          "instructions": "HDFC publishes no in-app MobileBanking or NetBanking UPI lock. Bank-side deactivation: 'banks do not facilitate the removal of UPI IDs directly from their mobile applications. If you wish to remove the IDs, visit your bank branch and submit a UPI deactivation request.' Fastest self-service freeze: deregister in your UPI app — 'Under settings, you will find the deregister option; click on it' and confirm; 'Once you confirm deregistration, your bank account will be unlinked from the UPI app' (re-linking later creates a new UPI ID). Unauthorised UPI transactions: 'To report any unauthorised Credit Card, Debit Card, NetBanking, or UPI transactions, please call 1800 258 6161' — have mobile number, Customer ID, account number, transaction date/time and amount ready. Compromised UPI account: 'quickly update your UPI PIN and contact your bank. You may also need to disable UPI transactions if necessary.' Partner-app customer care published by HDFC: Google Pay 1-800-419-0157, WhatsApp 1-800-212-8552, Mobikwik 011-61266390. No SMS/USSD (*99#) UPI block keyword published on HDFC pages. Current official app listings, verified live 2026-11-01 on the bank's MobileBanking app page: Android com.hdfcbank.android.now and iOS id6504402552 ('HDFC Bank App: Banking & Cards', seller HDFC Bank Ltd — the page publishes the /us/ form of the same listing; both fetched HTTP 200). The app itself offers no UPI freeze. Pre-existing credit/debit androidApp/iosApp links com.hdfcbank.mobile and id657927626 verified dead 2026-11-01 (HTTP 404; iTunes lookup resultCount 0), as are blog links com.snapwork.hdfc and id515891771 — those sections need Loop 2 re-verification.",
